build-meta/

# Environment variables — ignore every .env variant (incl. .env.development,
# services/edge-functions/.env, etc.) but keep the tracked placeholder examples.
# (US-272)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Placeholder template for the staging edge env (US-520) — no real values.
!.env.staging.example
# EXCEPTION: .env.production is committed on purpose — it holds the React app's
# build-time VITE_* vars for the Cloudflare Pages build (Pages can't read them
# from wrangler.toml). Every VITE_* value is PUBLIC by design (it's baked into
# the browser JS bundle), so committing it exposes nothing new. NEVER put a
# server secret (service-role key, Stripe secret, Anthropic key, webhook
# secrets) in this file — secrets must NOT be VITE_-prefixed and belong in the
# edge service env / Pages secrets only.
!.env.production

